=== ATS-102 evidence: the installed-tree digest does not depend on the checkout line-ending style ===
date  : 2026-11-05T09:25:15Z
commit: 912bee6  fix(ATS-102): 让安装树摘要与检出的换行风格无关
repo  : C:/Users/seiko/multica_workspaces_desktop-api.multica.ai/triton-n4hv-4bc6c5b98085/seikoist-14-43971fe3dca4/worktree

TWO fresh clones of the SAME commit are installed with the SAME npm, and
the digest is measured in each:

  clone A: core.autocrlf=true   -> the working tree gets CRLF (Windows default)
  clone B: core.autocrlf=false  -> the working tree stays LF

The digest recipe hashes TEXT files with their line endings normalised to
LF and BINARY files byte for byte, so the two clones must agree.

The line-ending style of the checkout is set per clone with
  git -c core.autocrlf=true  clone ... / git -c core.autocrlf=false clone ...
and the setting is re-applied after the clone, because git records the
config of the machine that made the clone, not the one passed on the
command line.

